  abstract: "EVERYTHING to solid is a free (non-commercial), offline program that turns an STL mesh, which is a bag of triangles, into a STEP solid, which is the kind of file a CAD program can edit: true planes, cylinders, spheres, surfaces of revolution and smooth NURBS patches, closed into one watertight body. This paper puts every method the program uses, with its parameters and its variants, into the public record, so that nobody can later patent them and stop people using them. It covers seventeen disclosures. The largest are:"
